        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): strip attachments >10MB before send to prevent HTTP 413 silent message loss (fixes #99021)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #99021.\n\nWhen an agent reply includes a media attachment larger than Discord's bot upload limit (10 MB), the entire outbound reply (text AND attachment) is rejected with HTTP 413 and silently lost. The run is logged as `outcome=completed`, no retry occurs, and the user sees the agent as simply not responding.\n\n## Changes Made\n\n- `extensions/discord/src/send.shared.ts`: Added `DISCORD_BOT_ATTACHMENT_LIMIT_BYTES = 10MB` constant and pre-flight size check in `sendDiscordMedia`. When attachment exceeds 10MB, it is stripped and text-only fallback is sent instead.\n- `extensions/discord/src/send.outbound.ts`: Lowered `DEFAULT_DISCORD_MEDIA_MAX_MB` from 100 to 10 to match Discord's actual bot limit.\n- `extensions/discord/src/send.sends-basic-channel-messages.test.ts`: Added regression test for oversized media.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real Discord API proof (live bot, redacted)\n\n```\n================================================\n DISCORD 413 FIX — REAL API VERIFICATION\n Time: 2026-07-02T11:02:36+00:00\n Host: LIN-66D8BD4EA2C\n================================================\n\nBEFORE FIX: 11MB attachment via Discord API\n  HTTP 413 — DISCARDED (message + attachment both lost)\n\nAFTER FIX: Size check → text delivered, no attachment\n  HTTP: 201\n  Message ID: 1522195816796782666\n  Content: \"Check this video\\n\\n_Attachment exceeds Discord's 10 MB limit...\"\n  Attachments: 0\n  ✅ TEXT DELIVERED, no attachment lost\n```\n\n### Unit tests (45/45 passed)\n```\n✓ strips oversized media >10MB and sends text-only fallback (#99021)\n✓ uploads media attachments\n✓ uses configured discord mediaMaxMb for uploads\n✓ 45 passed\n```\n\n## AI Assistance\n\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n- **Human confirmed understanding**: Yes",
